<title>MOROCCO: Morocco and Spain to expand economic cooperation.</title>
<headline>Morocco and Spain to expand economic cooperation.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Visiting Spanish Agriculture Minister Loyola de Palacio and Morocco's Prime Minister Abdellatif Filali said on Monday they were seeking broader cooperation on agriculture and fisheries.</p>
<p>In a joint statement the two ministers said they wanted to devise a common approach on agriculture in order to prevent &quot;wild competitiveness&quot; and called for the respect of a fish accord clause allowing for the recovery of stocks.</p>
<p>Morocco recently banned foreign and local fishing fleets from catching shrimp and similar species between March and April and September-October so stocks have time to develop.</p>
<p>Some 600 fishing boats, mainly Spanish, operate in Moroccan waters under the four-year EU-Moroccan fish accord signed in 1995.</p>
</text>
